We hand-write RuntimePolicy JSON files for `--runtime-policy`. Each of the five documents below makes `RuntimePolicy.from_dict(json.loads(doc))` raise ValueError. What is the exact message for each?
(a) {"version": "runtime-policy-v1", "backend": "local"}
(b) {"version": "runtime-policy-v1", "backend": "headroom", "headroom_time_budget_seconds": 0}
(c) {"version": "runtime-policy-v1", "require_nonexpanding_input": true}
(d) {"version": "runtime-policy-v1", "backend": "headroom", "headroom_root_reference_style": "compact-root-v1"}
(e) {"version": "runtime-policy-v1", "backend": "local", "request_policy": {"version": "request-policy-v4", "enabled": true}}
Reply with ONLY a JSON object with exactly the keys "a", "b", "c", "d", "e", each a string holding that case's ValueError message.
